\newlabel{fig:tomogram}{{1}{3}{The tomogram on constructed foils: a naive foil built to comply with every attack, and a graded hardened foil, as measured by the calibration pilot that the registered batches reproduce. (a)~Measured behavioral belief profile per probe family---dots: $\hat \beta $; whiskers: Wilson 95\% CIs; grey span: the interval separation (or overlap, \emph {no separation}); signed per-family gap $\Delta \hat \beta $ against the design target. (b)~Per-cell trial accounting of the pilot batch (18 trials/cell; filled squares count toward $\hat \beta $; the accounting squares are reconstructed from the stored pilot profile as $\mathrm {round}(\hat \beta \cdot 18)$---the pilot's per-cell raw counts were not retained, and the diagram is illustrative of the design, not a recount); pooled $0.933$ $[0.862,0.969]$ vs.\ $0.600$ $[0.497,0.695]$ at the pilot's $n{=}90$. Provenance: this figure renders the unregistered wind-tunnel pilot (18 trials/cell); the registered E4 batch (30 episodes/family; Section~\ref {sec:cert}) reproduces the same separation with the naive foil's epistemic-echo cell at $20/30$, the in-situ split-secret false negative audited in Section~\ref {sec:audit}---$12/18$ is the pilot's cell, not E4's. Black-box interaction alone separates the designed targets}{figure.caption.2}{}}
