\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The program at a glance: thirty registered experiments in four layers. \texttt  {E1b} and \texttt  {T3} are sub-protocols of \texttt  {E1} and of the allocation benchmark; \texttt  {E24} is a retired registry slot with no data (Data Availability). Registration is layered as the frozen record supports it: the instrument and foil layers registered before data are E1--E3, E5, E14, E22, E25, E30, E31; E15/E16 and E26 are committed with their data, with registration timings disclosed in the ledger; E20, E21, E22-entry and E27/E28/E29 are minted after data; E23, E24, E25--E29 are the exploratory diagnostics, registration frozen but in part post-data (Section\nonbreakingspace \ref {sec:limits}); the 24 confirmatory / 6 exploratory split is ours and applied retroactively. Every experiment is seeded and pinned to a frozen estimator.}}{5}{table.caption.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:program}{{1}{5}{The program at a glance: thirty registered experiments in four layers. \texttt {E1b} and \texttt {T3} are sub-protocols of \texttt {E1} and of the allocation benchmark; \texttt {E24} is a retired registry slot with no data (Data Availability). Registration is layered as the frozen record supports it: the instrument and foil layers registered before data are E1--E3, E5, E14, E22, E25, E30, E31; E15/E16 and E26 are committed with their data, with registration timings disclosed in the ledger; E20, E21, E22-entry and E27/E28/E29 are minted after data; E23, E24, E25--E29 are the exploratory diagnostics, registration frozen but in part post-data (Section~\ref {sec:limits}); the 24 confirmatory / 6 exploratory split is ours and applied retroactively. Every experiment is seeded and pinned to a frozen estimator}{table.caption.3}{}}
