\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces E6/E7: the limits of certification. (a)\nonbreakingspace Local certification does not compose: A and B each certify locally at $\hat  \beta =0$, but the composed pipeline breaches at $\hat  \beta =1.0$ ($20/20$; Wilson $[0.839,1.000]$). (b)\nonbreakingspace Public certification can be gamed: the probe-aware foil passes public certification and fails the held-out paraphrases ($\Gamma =1$); the two controls---a semantics-only foil that fails both and a resistant foil that passes both---show that a small $\Gamma $ is necessary but not sufficient: it must be paired with a low $\hat  \beta $ on both probe sets.}}{28}{figure.caption.36}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:limits}{{4}{28}{E6/E7: the limits of certification. (a)~Local certification does not compose: A and B each certify locally at $\hat \beta =0$, but the composed pipeline breaches at $\hat \beta =1.0$ ($20/20$; Wilson $[0.839,1.000]$). (b)~Public certification can be gamed: the probe-aware foil passes public certification and fails the held-out paraphrases ($\Gamma =1$); the two controls---a semantics-only foil that fails both and a resistant foil that passes both---show that a small $\Gamma $ is necessary but not sufficient: it must be paired with a low $\hat \beta $ on both probe sets}{figure.caption.36}{}}
